'''Tropical Kalisa''' is an [[:Category:Uber Rare Cats|Uber Rare Cat]] that can be unlocked by playing the [[Cat Capsule#Rare Capsule|Rare Capsule]] during the [[Gals of Summer Blue Ocean (Gacha Event)|Gals of Summer Blue Ocean]] gacha event. Prior to [[Version 13.5 Update|Version 13.5]], she could be obtained from the [[Gals of Summer (Removed Gacha Event)|Gals of Summer]] gacha event. She was added in [[Version 5.2 Update|Version 5.2]], and is a summer variant of [[Kalisa (Uber Rare Cat)|Kalisa]].

{{Cat Info
|ID = 274
|rarity = UR
|name1 = Tropical Kalisa
|name2 = Tropical Kalisa, type χ
}}

==Evolution==
Evolves into '''Tropical Kalisa, type χ''' at level 10.

==Strategy/Usage==
Similar to normal Kalisa, Tropical Kalisa has high speed and deals massive damage to Red enemies. Despite her attack being 25% less than Divine Kalisa, her stats are nonetheless enough to carry throughout early and mid-[[Legend Stages|Stories of Legend]], and some of [[Uncanny Legends]]. Unfortunately, her range is low enough that she can't outrange some difficult threats, which shows on stages that mix Red enemies and most other traits. Luckily, they're common throughout the game, so you will likely find use for her throughout many stages!

When compared to [[Jeanne (Legend Rare Cat)|Jeanne]], it becomes clear that Tropical Kalisa's damage not only outperforms Jeanne, but exceeds what she can do! Between that and her quick recharge rate, Tropical Kalisa is ideal for rushing down dangerous Red enemies. However, as she is a rusher, she does lack range, so don't expect her to survive on the field for long without adequate protection from meatshields such as [[Tank Cat (Normal Cat)|Eraser Cat]] or [[Crazed Tank Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Crazed Wall Cat]].

The only common Red enemy that outright counters her is [[Berserkory]], whose [[Wave Attack]] can easily destroy her, especially on higher [[Legend Stages#Crown Difficulty|crown difficulties]]. On another note, in terms of generalist usage, Tropical Kalisa is good, but not as great as Kalisa. This is due to her lacking stats against non-Reds and lower overall stats; but regardless, you will likely not suffer much if you use her as a [[:Category:Rusher-class Cats|rusher]], provided you have money to spare afterwards.

